Phase 10 audio offload requires hardware programming primitives for the
WaveBlaster (MPU-401) and OPL3 (YMF262) backends, plus a coordination
API for the SB16 audio-IRQ idle-pause mechanism. This patch adds the
helper API + state in two new files; patch 0038 modifies the SB16 audio
backend to use them.

New files:

- src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.h — public API contract:
  * MPU-401: Init/WriteByte/Shutdown/GetBLASTERPort
  * OPL3: Detect/InitChip/Shutdown/WriteRegister/WriteRegisterBlock/
    VoiceRegOffsets/VoiceWritePatch/VoiceNoteOn/VoiceNoteOff
  * Idle-pause: RegisterIdlePauseCallback/SetIdlePauseEnabled/
    ForcePause/ForceResume + SDL_DOSIdlePauseCallback typedef
  * Per-block extern counters (uint32_t µs/count, atomic on x86):
    doskutsu_audio_irq_wall_us / _irq_count / _sfx_active_count

- src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c — implementations:
  * MPU-401: reset+ACK probe at Init (10 ms timeout); UART-mode entry
    via 0x3F to command port; per-byte poll on bit 6 of status before
    data write; BLASTER env parser for `Pxxxx` field with 0x330 default
  * OPL3: canonical Adlib timer-1 detection (s1=0x00 → s2=0xC0); register
    write helper with bank routing (0x388/0x389 vs 0x38A/0x38B for
    secondary bank) + 6-dummy-status-read inter-write delay; voice
    register offset table for all 18 voices in 9-channel 2-op mode
    layout (per § D.5 design recommendation); OPL3-mode init via
    register 0x105 = 0x01 + 4-op disable via register 0x104 = 0x00
  * Idle-pause: state vars exposed to SB16 backend (patch 0038 services
    the request flags + DSP pause/resume command issuing); callback
    slot for engine-side counter accumulation

Engine consumes via `vendor/nxengine-evo/src/sound/AudioBackendWB.cpp`
and `AudioBackendOPL3.cpp` (nx-engine's lane, slot 0100+).

Per CLAUDE.md threading-zero invariant: all helpers synchronous /
blocking. No threads, no DPMI thunks beyond port-I/O primitives.

Per kbd-counter precedent (patches 0023+0025): uint32_t volatile
externs, atomic single-bus-cycle reads on x86 — no cli/sti.

Per `audio_mix_zero_is_not_audio_off.md`: idle-pause is the essential
lever for the projected ~12 ms / flip wall-clock removal during silent
gameplay (IRQ entry/exit cost, not mix work).

CMakeLists.txt unchanged: src/core/dos/*.c is globbed.

Design contract: docs/PHASE10-DESIGN.md § C / § D / § E.6 (gitignored).
Instrumentation contract: docs/PHASE10-CONTRACT.md (gitignored).
